      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1365760413,
      "text": "Cucumis myriocarpus, the gooseberry cucumber, gooseberry gourd, paddy melon, mallee pear or prickly paddy melon, is a prostrate or climbing annual herb native to tropical and southern Africa. It has small, round, yellow-green or green-striped fruit with soft spines, small yellow flowers and deeply lobed, light green leaves. The melon occurs in disturbed soil and cleared or bare areas, and thrives on summer moisture."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Cucumis myriocarpus",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucumis_myriocarpus",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 226230490,
      "text": "Cucumis myriocarpus, le concombre groseille, est une espèce de plante à fleurs de la famille des Cucurbitaceae, originaire de l’est de l’Afrique australe. C'est une plante herbacée dont le fruit est une baie toxique."
    },
    "pt": {
